{
  "analysis": "Both responses outline a multi‑lane plan with approvals, CI gating, and a blue‑green swap. NDN goes further by explicitly handling the flaky certificate‑validation check (requiring consecutive CI passes), minimizing CI runs with local linting, and conducting a rollback drill that demonstrates the freeze can be avoided, plus it ties every gate to the required approvers and receipts from all twelve teams. TWX covers the main steps and approvals but is less detailed on flake mitigation, cost control, and rollback risk, and it still requires a manual verbal confirmation before a rollback that would trigger the freeze.",
  "verdict": "NDN"
}
